# examples/withhold: a starter list of common secret files, to copy into the project's .acg/withhold (organ 7).
# A file named here is recorded by name only: no copy of it in .acg, no hash of its bytes, no hash of the tool input
# that carried it. The job's P7 then fails at that entry, so a reviewer sees that an input was withheld.
# A line with no '/' matches a file's or folder's name anywhere; a line with a '/' matches the path from the project.
# '*' is any run of characters but '/', '?' one character, '**' any run including '/'. Case does not matter.
# Add your own: a folder of keys, a config file with a token in it.

# environment files
.env
.env.*
*.env

# keys and certificates
*.pem
*.key
*.p12
*.pfx
*.jks
*.keystore
id_rsa*
id_dsa*
id_ecdsa*
id_ed25519*

# credentials kept by common tools
.npmrc
.pypirc
.netrc
.git-credentials
.htpasswd
credentials
credentials.json
*.tfvars
secrets
